{"step_index":255,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-15T11:25:18Z","content":"All tasks across the 3 phases have been completed, verified with automated tests, and documented.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Completed Work\n\n#### 1. Phase 1: Chatbot Messaging Bug Fix\n- **Root Cause**: In `core/templates/core/index.html`, the send button and Enter key handler called `sendMessage()`, but the function was named `sendChatMessage()`. This threw an uncaught `ReferenceError: sendMessage is not defined` whenever a user attempted to send a message.\n- **Permission Fix**: Changed `permission_classes` on [`AIChatView`](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/core/views.py#L233-L330) from `[IsAuthenticated]` to `[AllowAny]`, allowing both logged-in users and guests to consult the AI Librarian.\n- **Frontend Messaging Pipeline**: Fixed function call, added dynamic typing indicators, auto-scroll, markdown formatting (bold, breaks), and quick suggestion chips.\n\n#### 2. Phase 2: Comprehensive Book Knowledge Base & Q&A\n- **Catalog Metadata & RAG**: Updated `AIChatView` to dynamically aggregate library statistics (total books, audiobook counts, distinct genres, authors) and inject the full catalog overview into the prompt.\n- **Targeted Retrieval**: When users ask questions about specific titles, authors, or plot summaries, the backend searches the database and feeds matching excerpts (`content[:2000]`) into Gemini AI.\n- **Quantitative Accuracy**: The bot accurately answers questions like *\"Kutubxonada nechta kitob bor?\"* (e.g. *\"Jami 38 ta kitob, 9 ta audio kitob\"*), *\"Qaysi audio kitoblar bor?\"*, and genre listings.\n- **Resilient Fallback**: Implemented an intelligent local catalog answering engine so that if the Gemini API key is missing or quota is exceeded, the chatbot still answers all questions from real database records.\n\n#### 3. Phase 3: Audiobook Support for Every Book\n- **Database Model**: Added `audio_file` (`models.FileField`) and `audiobook_url` (`models.URLField`) to [`Book`](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/core/models.py) along with a `has_audio` property. Generated and applied migration `0002_book_aud\n<truncated 1209 bytes>\niolet (`#8b5cf6`) and teal (`#03dac6`) glowing aesthetic with Plus Jakarta Sans typography.\n- **Live Search & Filters**: Instant debounce search by title, author, or genre, plus one-click *\"Faqat Audio Kitoblar\"* toggle.\n- **Persistent Bottom Audio Player**: Built-in HTML5 player bar with play/pause, 10s skip/rewind, interactive seekbar, speed toggle (0.75x–2.0x), and volume control.\n- **Reader Modal**: Dual-mode modal with PDF viewer and clean text reading mode.\n- **Admin Modals**: Forms for \"Yangi Kitob Qo'shish\" (Title, Author, Genre, PDF, Audio) and \"Audio Kitob Biriktirish\".\n- **Toast Alerts**: Non-blocking toast notifications replacing browser `alert()`.\n\n#### 6. Database Population & Startup\n- Created [`setup_library`](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/core/management/commands/setup_library.py) command which indexed all **38+ PDF books** from `media/books/` and seeded default accounts:\n  - **Admin**: `admin@library.com` / `admin123`\n  - **User**: `user@library.com` / `user123`\n- Updated [`run_project.py`](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/run_project.py) and [`requirements.txt`](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/requirements.txt) to automate migrations and server startup.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results\n1. **Django Test Suite (`manage.py test core`)**: **All 9 unit tests passed** in 35.8s.\n2. **Endpoint Tests (`test_api.py`)**: Registration (201), Login (200), Auth Me (200), Books (200), and Index View (200) **all passed**.\n3. **Live Permission Tests**:\n   - Regular user delete -> `403 Forbidden`\n   - Regular user audio upload -> `403 Forbidden`\n   - Admin audio upload -> `200 OK`\n   - Admin delete -> `204 No Content`\n4. **Live Chat Query**: Responded accurately with `38` books and `9` audiobooks.\n\nFor detailed walkthrough and documentation, see [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9b93b8e7-46ce-437a-8ae9-cea474183c38/walkthrough.md).\n\n### How to Run\n```powershell\n.\\venv\\Scripts\\python.exe run_project.py\n```\nOpen **`http://127.0.0.1:8000/`** in your browser.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
